viola-verify-<pid>-resume/`, loading the capture plugin from `ledger/probes/<pid>/resume/plugin/` and resuming Run B's first session with `--resume <id>`, no key typed. Runs B, C and D, as real interactive turns, also run the user's own global hooks, and Runs C and D, and Run B on Windows, the user's own status line (on Unix Run B's status line is the probe capture its one probe `--settings` names, [CLI Version Compatibility]), and each leaves the CLI's session transcripts under `~/.claude/projects/` (an accepted residual, security-plan Data Protection): Run B three per real-CLI verify, its session, the `<id>-backup-<n>.jsonl` the CLI writes at its pasted `/compact`'s compaction and the session its pasted `/clear` opens (the last inferred, not read), and C and D one each; Run E adds none (as measured on 2.1.287 at chunk 2026-10-18-compact-post-condition-ledger-row, `evidence/live-round.md`: the `viola-verify` transcript count 60 → 65).
