 - `VIOLA_NAME`: the instance's `ViolaName`. It is set by `viola run` in the child, and its absence makes every hook event path a silent exit 0 (the hidden `hook --capture` arm reads no `VIOLA_*` at all, [Hook Contract]).
-- `VIOLA_DIR`: the absolute path of the instance's state directory (`<viola home>/instances/<ViolaName>/`), set by `viola run` in the child. It is read by `hook` (for the recorded `endpoint`, the SessionEnd direct-append fallback, the statusline wrapper and the diagnostics directory) and by `mcp` and every CLI verb run inside the session. Each derives the viola home as the grandparent of `VIOLA_DIR`, so a session started with `--home` keeps its hooks, MCP server and nested CLI calls in that home. As landed (chunk 2026-10-17-cli-machine-contract), `hook` and every CLI verb, `run` and `revive` included, read it: the verbs through `resolved_home`, which takes the `VIOLA_DIR` grandparent only when `VIOLA_NAME` and `VIOLA_DIR` pass `instance_of`'s shape check, a pair that fails falling through to the default, never refusing (§Cross-cutting Patterns, Config management); `viola mcp` (chunk 2026-10-17-mcp-server-for-drivers) resolves its home through the same `resolved_home` and reads `VIOLA_NAME` for its own name (the `from` it adds and its detail sink). The CLI verbs' reading of it, and `mcp`'s through `resolved_home`, are NOT ratified: the founder's own word is owed (the Viola overseer's answer, a delegate's, `inputs#I3` of chunk 2026-10-17-cli-machine-contract; for `mcp`, the overseer's answer at the 2026-10-17-mcp-server-for-drivers wrap, a delegate's).
